{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,23]],"date-time":"2026-09-23T17:43:20Z","timestamp":1790185400865,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":28,"publisher":"IOP Publishing","issue":"11","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2018,11,19]],"date-time":"2018-11-19T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1542585600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":18,"URL":"https:\/\/publishingsupport.iopscience.iop.org\/iop-standard\/v1"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2018,11,19]],"date-time":"2018-11-19T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1542585600000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":18,"URL":"https:\/\/iopscience.iop.org\/info\/page\/text-and-data-mining"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100006769","name":"Russian Science Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","award":["14-22-00273"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["14-22-00273"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100006769","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"crossref"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["iopscience.iop.org"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Plasma Sources Sci. Technol."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2018,11,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    The initial stage of the fast electrical breakdown of an air gap with a pin-to-plane electrode geometry is studied on a nanosecond time scale using multi-frame laser probing with an exposure time of 70\u00a0ps and spatial resolution as high as 3\u20134\u00a0\n                    <jats:italic>\u03bc<\/jats:italic>\n                    m. We find that the gap breakdown is associated with the fast (\u22721 ns) formation of a micron-sized (\u223c10\n                    <jats:italic>\u03bc<\/jats:italic>\n                    m) cathode spot that appears as a plasma with an electron density of\n                    <jats:inline-formula>\n                      <jats:tex-math>\n                        \n                      <\/jats:tex-math>\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" overflow=\"scroll\">\n                        <mml:msub>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>e<\/mml:mi>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                        <\/mml:msub>\n                        <mml:mo>\u2248<\/mml:mo>\n                        <mml:msup>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mn>10<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mn>19<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                        <\/mml:msup>\n                        <mml:mspace width=\"0.25em\"\/>\n                        <mml:msup>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>cm<\/mml:mi>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>\u2212<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>3<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                        <\/mml:msup>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/jats:inline-formula>\n                    . The spot is then transformed into a spark channel having an electron density of\n                    <jats:inline-formula>\n                      <jats:tex-math>\n                        \n                      <\/jats:tex-math>\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" overflow=\"scroll\">\n                        <mml:msub>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>e<\/mml:mi>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                        <\/mml:msub>\n                        <mml:mo>\u223c<\/mml:mo>\n                        <mml:msup>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mn>10<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mn>19<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                        <\/mml:msup>\n                        <mml:mo>\u2013<\/mml:mo>\n                        <mml:msup>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mn>10<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mn>20<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                        <\/mml:msup>\n                        <mml:mspace width=\"0.25em\"\/>\n                        <mml:msup>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>cm<\/mml:mi>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>\u2212<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>3<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                        <\/mml:msup>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/jats:inline-formula>\n                    . Within \u223c1\u00a0ns after the breakdown the dynamics of the highly ionized near-cathode plasma governs the current capacity of the discharge gap as well as the current rise rate.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1088\/1361-6595\/aaebdb","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2018,10,26]],"date-time":"2018-10-26T18:45:16Z","timestamp":1540579516000},"page":"11LT01","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1088\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":43,"title":["Mechanisms responsible for the initiation of a fast breakdown in an atmospheric discharge"],"prefix":"10.1088","volume":"27","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003